cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Okanagan main valley lakes — 1971 chemical limnology (digitised from the
  Canada–British Columbia Okanagan Basin Agreement, Technical Supplement V)
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite both this transcription and the original
  1974 report it is derived from.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Jatel
    given-names: Nelson
    affiliation: Okanagan Basin Water Board
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # <- add if you have one
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Okanagan-Basin-Water-Board/ok-1974-limnology
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-03"
keywords:
  - limnology
  - Okanagan
  - British Columbia
  - phosphorus
  - water quality
  - historical baseline
  - data rescue
abstract: >-
  A verified transcription of Appendix C of the Canada–British Columbia Okanagan
  Basin Agreement (1974), Technical Supplement V: The Limnology of the Major
  Okanagan Basin Lakes. Contains 3,991 depth-resolved observations from six main
  valley lakes (Okanagan, Kalamalka, Wood, Skaha, Osoyoos, plus Vaseux
  morphometry), 21 stations and four 1971 cruises: nutrients (NO3, TKN,
  ortho-phosphate, total phosphate, silica) and major anions (bicarbonate,
  sulphate, chloride, fluoride), 1–220 m depth. This is the pre-EMS baseline for
  the Okanagan basin; the provincial in-situ record begins in the 1970s.
  Phosphorus is reported as PO4 in the source and as P in the report's policy
  table; both conventions are carried explicitly. Transcription is reconciled
  against the report's own published summary tables.
references:
  - type: report
    title: >-
      Technical Supplement V: The Limnology of the Major Okanagan Basin Lakes
    authors:
